      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Heart of Darkness\" is a dark novella chronicling a European voyage into the Congo, where the protagonist Marlow witnesses the moral decay and inherent savagery of colonialism. The novella thematically explores the corrupting nature of imperialism, examining the clash between civilization and primal instinct. The African characters are often portrayed as enigmatic entities or symbols of the unknowable darkness, which serves to critique the European obsession with \"civilizing\" the continent while masking oppressive exploitation.",
